<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Antonio Olañeta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1825</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Antonio Olañeta was a Spanish royalist general who commanded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-peru">Upper Peru</a>, present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, during the wars of independence. In 1824 he rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> La Serna, weakening the royalist cause before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ayacucho">Battle of Ayacucho</a>. He refused to surrender after that defeat and was killed at Tumusla in April 1825, ending Spanish resistance in Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-antonio-olaneta.jpg" alt="Pedro Antonio Olañeta" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olaneta1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
